{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>You shall not follow a majority for evil.</b> This verse has midrashim from the Sages of Israel, but the language of the verse does not settle properly in them. From here they derived: one does not incline toward liability by the vote of a single judge. And the end of the verse they derived: <b>after a majority to incline</b> — if there are two more voting liable than those voting acquittal, incline the verdict according to them toward liability — and it is capital cases the verse speaks of. And the middle of the verse they derived: <b>do not answer about a rav</b> — about a rav: one does not dissent against the most senior member of the court; therefore in capital cases they begin from the side — they ask the youngest among them first, so that they state their opinion — and according to our Rabbis the resolution of the verse is thus: <b>You shall not follow a majority for evil.</b> To impose the death penalty on account of a single judge — when the liable votes outnumber the acquittals — and <b>do not answer about the rav</b> to depart from his words. And because it is written deficient in yod, they derived this — <b>after a majority to incline</b>: there is a majority you do follow — and when? When there are two tipping the balance among those voting liable more than those voting acquittal. And from the implication of what is said — <b>you shall not follow a majority for evil</b> — I would hear: but do be with them for good; from here they said: in capital cases one inclines by one vote for acquittal and by two for liability. And Onkelos translated: לָא תִתְמְנַע מִלְּאַלָּפָא מָה דְּמִתְבְּעֵי לָךְ עַל דִּינָא — and the Hebrew, according to the translation, is expounded thus: <b>do not answer about a rav to incline.</b> If they ask you a matter of law, do not answer to incline to one side and withdraw yourself from the dispute — but judge it for its truth." "And I say to settle it in its proper sense according to its plain meaning — this is its resolution: <b>You shall not follow a majority for evil.</b> If you saw wicked men perverting justice, do not say: since they are a majority, I will incline after them." "<b>And you shall not answer about a rav to incline, etc.</b> And if the litigant asks you about that case, do not answer him regarding the dispute a word that follows that majority to pervert the judgment from its truth — but state the judgment as it is, and let the collar hang on the neck of the majority (Sanhedrin 7)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:10.348835706Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}